            },
            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nBefore using the mathematical tools presented in this text, we recommend studying the first five chapters of the *First Steps* section, which explain the mathematical operations these tools use (<htcite0>):",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "b5efc8f9-c268-430f-9681-7a43848ee48e",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "First steps (Volume 1)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Introduction\n\nGreat constructions were erected on the American continent (*Abya Yala*) that required logic and organizational skills, so it is reasonable to assume that Indigenous peoples possessed knowledge in areas that we now call sciences. In this text, we will explore two of their mathematical tools: the Inca *Yupana* from the Andes and the grids of Mesoamerica. With this in mind, we invite the reader to reflect:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: On mathematics</b><br /><br />Did Indigenous peoples develop skills to perform mathematical operations?</div></div></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "The answer is yes. This text brings together some of the tools presented in other chapters to show how Indigenous peoples performed mathematical operations with them.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_andes",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Mathematics in the Andes\n\nOur studies on the use of mathematics in the Andes have been based on the *Yupana Inka Tawa Pukllay* method, developed and published by Dhavit Prem (<htcite0>; <htcite1>) of the Yupanki Association.\n\n#### The Yupana\n\nThe *Yupana* is an instrument used by the Incas to perform calculations, functioning in a way similar to a calculator. Its name was deduced, as Professor Dhavit Prem explained in a conversation:",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "pp. 354 - 363",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "2d2ea4a5-506b-4dbf-aaa4-3a10a8fbbd9c",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<ul class=\"citation\"><li><i>\"Yupana does not appear in the texts of the chroniclers; they mention an instrument for counting, but the name itself is precise. Quechua is a language that allows the creation of neologisms that any speaker can understand. 'Yupai' is the verb in the infinitive meaning ‘to count’. By removing the final ‘i’ and adding the suffix -na, which means ‘that which serves for,’ we obtain yupana, that is, ‘that which serves for counting’.\"</i></li></ul>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "The *Yupana* was depicted by Felipe Guaman Poma de Ayala in his 16th-century work (by the Gregorian calendar), alongside quipus, which, in addition to accounting information, may also have contained written records that have not yet been deciphered (<htcite0>; <htcite1>):",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ce028897-f426-41a1-8406-4519011fa9ec",
                     "text": "Moras, Roberto",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "6ff52558-f4fb-49cd-a737-0e2f3863ae7b",
                     "text": "Laurencich Minelli, L.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2016",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgPoma\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgPoma', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Book 1</b>: Page 362, Felipe Guaman Poma de Ayala's book (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "f5b74f18-0bc4-46d2-8a5c-64dd80b74dd1",
                     "text": "Poma de Ayala, Felipe Guaman",
                     "page": "pp. 362",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1615",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "13"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2015",
                     "month": "4",
                     "day": "26"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "On this image, we see an Indigenous man holding a quipu (knotted cords), with a numerical value indicated on the right. To the left, there is a Yupana—a board with dots representing numbers, possibly associated with finger counting.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### Operations with the *Yupana*\n\nThe operations with the *Yupana* are explained in the *First Steps* section (<htcite0>; <htcite1>; <htcite2>).\n\nThe five movements have Quechua names: *ISKAY* (two), *KIMSA* (three), *PISQA* (five), *PICHANA* (broom), and *KINKIN* (equivalence).\n\nBelow, select the movement you wish to perform on the *yupana*, then use the arrow <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-left-right\" style=\"color:#0f0;\"></i> to move the circles and update the fingers on the hands, and the arrow <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate\" style=\"color:#00f;\"></i> to return to the original position:",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1bb0274d-dc51-4740-ac62-4d157b06ad88",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Yupana (Addition)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "c4c2c00d-7878-42da-9cc4-060cd7f8d225",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Yupana (multiplication)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "f17ec53f-af65-4708-bcc1-a140287d4dd9",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Subtracting with the Yupana",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><center><input type=\"radio\" value=\"0\" name=\"yupanaradio2\" /> <i>ISKAY</i> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\" name=\"yupanaradio2\" /> <i>KIMSA</i> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\" name=\"yupanaradio2\" /> <i>PISQA</i> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\" name=\"yupanaradio2\" /> <i>PICHANA</i> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"4\" name=\"yupanaradio2\" /> <i>KINKIN</i> </center></p><p><table id=\"yupana0\" class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"4\"><i>Yupana</i></th><th>Left Hand</th><th>Right Hand</th><th>Arrows</th></tr> <tr id=\"tf1\"><td id=\"tc1f1\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f1\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f1\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f1\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td><td id=\"tc5f1\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"leftHandImg3\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('leftHandImg3', '0%')\"  /></td><td id=\"tc5f1\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"rightHandImg3\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('rightHandImg3', '0%')\"  /></td><td id=\"tc7f1\" rowspan=\"2\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-left-right upArrowWithFA\" id=\"traineeUp3\"></i> <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate downArrowWithFA\" style=\"font-size:4em;color:#00f;\" id=\"traineeDown3\"></i></td><tr id=\"tf2\"><td id=\"tc1f2\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f2\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f2\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f2\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr></tr></table></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 1</b>: Representation of the movements of the <i>Yupana Inka Tawa Pukllay</i>. CSS inspired by W3Schools <htcite0> code.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "48dd9187-7ecc-4f54-a387-d9ecc2497de3",
                     "text": "W3School",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "01",
                        "day": "27"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### Reverse movements with the *Yupana*\n\nThe same movements are used to subtract on the *yupana*, but performed in reverse order. On the *Yupana*, subtraction is known as *T'aqay*, or parallel subtraction (<htcite0>).\n\nBelow, select the movement you wish to perform in reverse on the *yupana*, then use the arrow <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-left-right\" style=\"color:#0f0;\"></i> to move the circles and update the fingers on the hands, and the arrow <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate\" style=\"color:#00f;\"></i> to return to the original position:\n",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "f17ec53f-af65-4708-bcc1-a140287d4dd9",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Subtracting with the Yupana",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><center><input type=\"radio\" value=\"0\" name=\"yupanaradio3\" /> <i>ISKAY</i> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"1\" name=\"yupanaradio3\" /> <i>KIMSA</i> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"2\" name=\"yupanaradio3\" /> <i>PISQA</i> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"3\" name=\"yupanaradio3\" /> <i>PICHANA</i> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"4\" name=\"yupanaradio3\" /> <i>KINKIN</i> </center></p><p><p><table id=\"yupana2\" class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"4\"><i>Yupana</i></th><th>Left Hand</th><th>Right Hand</th><th>Arrows</th></tr> <tr id=\"tf1\"><td id=\"tc1f1\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f1\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f1\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f1\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td><td id=\"tc5f1\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"leftHandImg4\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('leftHandImg4', '0%')\"  /></td><td id=\"tc6f1\" rowspan=\"2\"><img id=\"rightHandImg4\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('rightHandImg4', '0%')\"  /></td><td id=\"tc7f1\" rowspan=\"2\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-left-right upArrowWithFA\" id=\"traineeUp4\"></i> <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate downArrowWithFA\" style=\"font-size:4em;color:#00f;\" id=\"traineeDown4\"></i></td></tr> <tr id=\"tf2\"><td id=\"tc1f2\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f2\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f2\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f2\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr></table></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 2</b>: Representation of the inverse movements of the <i>Yupana Inka Tawa Pukllay</i>. CSS inspired by <htcite0> code.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "48dd9187-7ecc-4f54-a387-d9ecc2497de3",
                     "text": "W3School",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "01",
                        "day": "27"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### Practicing with the *Yupana*\n\nNow it is your turn. Use the selector below to choose the operation you want to practice: **Add**, **Multiply**, or **Subtract**. The app will propose a calculation and guide you through each step on a Yupana with four rows, where each row represents one digit (from 0 to 9).\n\nUse **New Exercise** to start another calculation, **Next Level** to change the difficulty, **Reset** to restart the current calculation, and **Next Step** to continue after completing each stage. At the end, the result is shown on the Yupana.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<style>.yupana-panel { background: #2e241f; border-radius: 50px; padding: 8px 18px; margin-bottom: 15px; margin-top: 15px; box-shadow: inset 0 2px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.4), 0 3px 6px rgba(255,245,190,0.3); } .yupana-panel .exercise-header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; } .level-badge { background: #ffb347; color: #1f2a0e; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 30px; font-size: clamp(0.8rem, 3vw, 1rem); white-space: nowrap; } .problem-display { background: #f2ecd8; padding: 4px 16px; border-radius: 35px; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 1.5rem); color: #1f2a0e; white-space: nowrap; } .ex-btn { background: #846b4e; border: none; color: #ffefcf; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 2.5vw, 0.9rem); font-family: inherit; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 50px; cursor: pointer; transition: 0.2s; } .ex-btn:hover { background: #a58a6a; transform: scale(1.03); } .ex-btn.hidden { display: none; } .step-panel { padding: 8px 0; color: #ffefcf; font-size: clamp(0.8rem, 2.5vw, 1rem); } .step-status { font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 2vw, 0.85rem); opacity: 0.9; margin-top: 4px; color: #ffefcf; } .feedback-area { text-align: center; margin: 10px 0; font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 3vw, 1.2rem); } .congrats { color: #2e7d32; font-weight: bold; } .success-message { color: #fff; } .next-step-btn { display: block; margin: 10px auto; background: #2e7d32; border: none; color: white; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 3vw, 1.1rem); font-family: inherit; padding: 10px 30px; border-radius: 50px; cursor: pointer; transition: 0.2s; } .next-step-btn:hover { background: #388e3c; transform: scale(1.03); } .next-step-btn.hidden { display: none; } #yupana1 { zoom: 0.7; }</style><p><center><input type=\"radio\" value=\"sum\" name=\"yupanaop\" checked=\"checked\" /> <b>Add</b> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"mult\" name=\"yupanaop\" /> <b>Multiply</b> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"sub\" name=\"yupanaop\" /> <b>Subtract</b></center></p><p><table id=\"yupana1\" class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"4\"><i>Yupana</i></th></tr> <tr id=\"tf1\"><td id=\"tc1f1\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f1\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f1\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f1\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr> <tr id=\"tf2\"><td id=\"tc1f2\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f2\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f2\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f2\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr> <tr id=\"tf3\"><td id=\"tc1f3\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f3\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f3\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f3\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr> <tr id=\"tf4\"><td id=\"tc1f4\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f4\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f4\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f4\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td></tr></table></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 3</b>: <i>Yupana</i>. CSS inspired in <htcite0> code.</p><div class=\"yupana-panel\"><div class=\"exercise-header\"><span class=\"level-badge\" id=\"levelBadge\">🔢 Units</span><span class=\"problem-display\" id=\"problemDisplay\">512 + 513</span><button class=\"ex-btn\" id=\"resetTutorBtn\">🎲 New Exercise</button><button class=\"ex-btn\" id=\"nextLevelBtn\">⭐ Next Level</button></div><button class=\"ex-btn\" id=\"resetButton\">↺ Reset</button><div class=\"step-panel\" id=\"stepMessage\">🧮 Click 'New exercise' to start</div><div class=\"step-status\" id=\"stepStatus\"></div><div class=\"feedback-area\" id=\"feedbackArea\"></div><div class=\"mult-table\" id=\"multTable\"></div><button class=\"next-step-btn\" id=\"nextStepBtn\">➡️ Next Step</button></div><div class=\"text-store\" style=\"display:none;\"><span id=\"add_txt_stepPrefix\">🧮</span><span id=\"add_txt_correctMessage\">✅ Correct! Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"add_txt_movementISKAY\">ISKAY</span><span id=\"add_txt_movementKIMSA\">KIMSA</span><span id=\"add_txt_movementPISQA\">PISQA</span><span id=\"add_txt_movementPICHANA\">PICHANA</span><span id=\"add_txt_movementKINKIN\">KINKIN</span><span id=\"add_txt_movementsMessage\">✅ Correct! Movement(s) performed in {placeName}: <strong>{movements}</strong>. Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"add_txt_noMovementsMessage\">✅ Correct! No movement needed in {placeName}. Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"add_txt_carryConfirmMessage\">✅ Correct! The carried <strong>1</strong> was placed in {nextPlace} (<strong>{movements}</strong>). Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"add_txt_carrying\">carrying</span><span id=\"add_txt_perfectMessage\">🎉🎉🎉 PERFECT! 🎉🎉🎉<br>{a} + {b} = {result}<br>Great job using the Yupana!</span><span id=\"add_txt_congratsMessage\">🎉🎉🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! 🎉🎉🎉<br>You calculated {a} + {b} = {result}<br>Click 'New exercise' to practice more!</span><span id=\"add_txt_finalLevelMessage\">🎉🏆 ALL LEVELS COMPLETE! 🏆🎉<br>You mastered addition on the Yupana! Click \"New exercise\" to start again at level 1.</span><span id=\"add_txt_lastLevelMessage\">🏅 Congratulations! You reached the last level! 🏅</span><span id=\"add_txt_step1Instruction\">📌 <strong>Step 1:</strong> Set the first number <strong>{a}</strong> by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"add_txt_step2Instruction\">📌 <strong>Step 2:</strong> Set the second number <strong>{b}</strong> by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"add_txt_step1DigitInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Set the <strong>{digit}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares of that row.</span><span id=\"add_txt_step2DigitInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Set the <strong>{digit}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares of that row.</span><span id=\"add_txt_simpleAddInstruction\">➕ <strong>Add to {placeName}:</strong> Add <strong>{digit}</strong> to the {placeName}. The {placeName} should become <strong>{result}</strong>.</span><span id=\"add_txt_carryInstruction\">⚡ <strong>Carry in {placeName}:</strong> Adding <strong>{digit}</strong> to {placeName} gives {digitA} + {digit} = {total}, which exceeds 9. Add the extra <strong>1</strong> to <strong>{nextPlace}</strong>. The {placeName} should become <strong>{resultDigit}</strong>.</span><span id=\"add_txt_evalCarry\">⚡ <strong>Carry in {placeName}:</strong> {digitA} + {digitB} = {total}, which exceeds 9. Add the extra <strong>1</strong> to <strong>{nextPlace}</strong>. The {placeName} should become <strong>{resultDigit}</strong>.</span><span id=\"add_txt_evalSimple\">➕ <strong>Resolve {placeName}:</strong> {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{result}</strong>. Place <strong>{result}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"add_txt_evalCarryDigit\">⚡ <strong>Resolve {placeName}:</strong> {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{total}</strong>. Place <strong>{resultDigit}</strong> in the {placeName}.</span><span id=\"add_txt_evalZero\">⚡ <strong>{placeName} will be {total}:</strong> {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{total}</strong>. Since the result in the row is <strong>0</strong>, you don't need to place anything on the Yupana.</span><span id=\"add_txt_carryFinalInstruction\">➕ Add the carried <strong>1</strong> to the next column by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"add_txt_finalInstruction\">🎉 <strong>Verify:</strong> {a} + {b} = <strong>{result}</strong>. The markers on the Yupana should match this result.</span><span id=\"add_txt_stepStatus\">📖 Step {current}/{total}</span><span id=\"add_txt_readyStatus\">🎲 Ready</span><span id=\"add_txt_welcomeMessage\">Click 'New exercise' to start. Click on the Yupana rows to arrange the number.</span><span id=\"add_txt_overflowMessage\">⚠️ <strong>Overflow!</strong> The {place} row has a value of {digit}, which exceeds the maximum of 9. Each Yupana line can only represent digits from 0 to 9. Clear some markers and try again.</span><span id=\"add_txt_units\">Units</span><span id=\"add_txt_tens\">Tens</span><span id=\"add_txt_hundreds\">Hundreds</span><span id=\"add_txt_thousands\">Thousands</span><span id=\"add_txt_levelUnits\">🔢 Units</span><span id=\"add_txt_levelTens\">🔟 Tens</span><span id=\"add_txt_levelHundreds\">🏆 Hundreds</span><span id=\"add_txt_next\">next</span><span id=\"mult_txt_level\">✖ Multiply by</span><span id=\"mult_txt_stepPrefix\">🧮</span><span id=\"mult_txt_correctMessage\">✅ Correct! Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_movementISKAY\">ISKAY</span><span id=\"mult_txt_movementKIMSA\">KIMSA</span><span id=\"mult_txt_movementPISQA\">PISQA</span><span id=\"mult_txt_movementPICHANA\">PICHANA</span><span id=\"mult_txt_movementKINKIN\">KINKIN</span><span id=\"mult_txt_movementsMessage\">✅ Correct! Movement(s) performed in {placeName}: <strong>{movements}</strong>. Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_noMovementsMessage\">✅ Correct! No movement needed in {placeName}. Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_carryConfirmMessage\">✅ Correct! The carried <strong>1</strong> was placed in {nextPlace}, shown in <strong>red on the opposite side</strong> (<strong>{movements}</strong>). Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_carrying\">carrying</span><span id=\"mult_txt_perfectMessage\">🎉🎉🎉 PERFECT! 🎉🎉🎉<br>{value} × {times} = {result}<br>Great job using the Yupana!</span><span id=\"mult_txt_congratsMessage\">🎉🎉🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! 🎉🎉🎉<br>You calculated {value} × {times} = {result}<br>Click 'New exercise' to practice more!</span><span id=\"mult_txt_finalLevelMessage\">🎉🏆 ALL LEVELS COMPLETE! 🏆🎉<br>You mastered multiplication on the Yupana! Click 'New exercise' to start again at level 1.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_lastLevelMessage\">🏅 Congratulations! You reached the last level! 🏅</span><span id=\"mult_txt_step1Instruction\">📌 <strong>Step 1:</strong> Set the first value <strong>{value}</strong> by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_step2Instruction\">📌 <strong>Step 2:</strong> Add the value <strong>{value}</strong> by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_step1DigitInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Set the <strong>{digit}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares of that row.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_step2DigitInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Add the <strong>{digit}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares of that row.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_evalSimple\">➕ <strong>Step {step}:</strong> {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{result}</strong>. Place <strong>{result}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_evalCarryDigit\">⚡ <strong>Step {step}:</strong> {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{total}</strong>. Place <strong>{resultDigit}</strong> in the {placeName}.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_evalZero\">⚡ <strong>Step {step}:</strong> {placeName} will be {total}: {digitA} + {digitB} = <strong>{total}</strong>. Since the result in the row is <strong>0</strong>, you don't need to place anything on the Yupana.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_carryFinalInstruction\">➕ <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Add the carried <strong>1</strong> to the next column by clicking on the Yupana squares. It will appear in <strong>red on the opposite side</strong>.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_finalInstruction\">🎉 <strong>Verify:</strong> {value} × {times} = <strong>{result}</strong>. The markers on the Yupana should match this result.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_stepStatus\">📖 Step {current}/{total}</span><span id=\"mult_txt_welcomeMessage\">Click 'New exercise' to start. Click on the Yupana rows to arrange the value.</span><span id=\"mult_txt_units\">Units</span><span id=\"mult_txt_tens\">Tens</span><span id=\"mult_txt_hundreds\">Hundreds</span><span id=\"mult_txt_thousands\">Thousands</span><span id=\"mult_txt_next\">next</span><span id=\"sub_txt_stepPrefix\">🧮</span><span id=\"sub_txt_movementISKAY\">ISKAY</span><span id=\"sub_txt_movementKIMSA\">KIMSA</span><span id=\"sub_txt_movementPISQA\">PISQA</span><span id=\"sub_txt_movementPICHANA\">PICHANA</span><span id=\"sub_txt_movementCANCEL\">CANCEL</span><span id=\"sub_txt_inverse\">inverse</span><span id=\"sub_txt_as\">as</span><span id=\"sub_txt_correctMessage\">✅ Correct! Click <strong>Next Step</strong> to continue.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_movementsMessage\">✅ Correct! Movement(s) performed in the {placeName}: <strong>{movements}</strong>. Click <strong>Next Step</strong> to continue.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_noMovementsMessage\">✅ Correct! No movement is needed in the {placeName}. Click <strong>Next Step</strong> to continue.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_borrowConfirmMessage\">✅ Correct! You borrowed <strong>1</strong> from the {nextPlace}. Click <strong>Next Step</strong> to continue.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_borrowing\">borrowing</span><span id=\"sub_txt_perfectMessage\">🎉🎉🎉 PERFECT! 🎉🎉🎉<br>{a} − {b} = {result}<br>Great job using the Yupana!</span><span id=\"sub_txt_congratsMessage\">🎉🎉🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! 🎉🎉🎉<br>You calculated {a} − {b} = {result}<br>Click <strong>New Exercise</strong> to practice more!</span><span id=\"sub_txt_finalLevelMessage\">🎉🏆 ALL LEVELS COMPLETE! 🏆🎉<br>You mastered subtraction on the Yupana! Click <strong>New Exercise</strong> to start again at level 1.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_lastLevelMessage\">🏅 Congratulations! You reached the last level! 🏅</span><span id=\"sub_txt_step1Instruction\">📌 <strong>Step 1:</strong> Set the first number <strong>{a}</strong> by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_step2Instruction\">📌 <strong>Step 2:</strong> Set the second number <strong>{b}</strong> by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_step1DigitInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Set the digit <strong>{digit}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the squares of that row.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_step2DigitInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> Set the digit <strong>{digit}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the squares of that row.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_evalSimple\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> ➖ <strong>Solve the {placeName}:</strong> {digitA} − {digitB} = <strong>{result}</strong>. Place <strong>{result}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_evalBorrow\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> ⚡ <strong>Solve the {placeName}:</strong> After borrowing, {digitA} + 10 − {digitB} = <strong>{result}</strong>. Place <strong>{result}</strong> in the {placeName} by clicking on the Yupana squares.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_evalZero\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> ➖ <strong>The {placeName} will be 0:</strong> {digitA} − {digitB} = <strong>{result}</strong>. Because the result in this row is <strong>0</strong>, the markers cancel each other out.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_evalNine\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> 🎉 <strong>The {placeName} will be {result}:</strong> After borrowing, {digitA} + 10 − {digitB} = <strong>{result}</strong>. The result was placed automatically.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_borrowInstruction\">📌 <strong>Step {step}:</strong> ⚡ <strong>Borrow from the {nextPlace}:</strong> {digitA} − {digitB} cannot be done in the {placeName}. Rewrite {rewriteList} with red markers.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_finalInstruction\">🎉 <strong>Check the result:</strong> {a} − {b} = <strong>{result}</strong>. The markers on the Yupana should match this result.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_stepStatus\">📖 Step {current}/{total}</span><span id=\"sub_txt_readyStatus\">🎲 Ready</span><span id=\"sub_txt_welcomeMessage\">Click <strong>New Exercise</strong> to start. Click the Yupana rows to set the number.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_overflowMessage\">⚠️ <strong>Overflow!</strong> The {place} row has a value of {digit}, which is greater than 9. Each Yupana row can only represent digits from 0 to 9. Clear some markers and try again.</span><span id=\"sub_txt_units\">units</span><span id=\"sub_txt_tens\">tens</span><span id=\"sub_txt_hundreds\">hundreds</span><span id=\"sub_txt_thousands\">thousands</span><span id=\"sub_txt_levelUnits\">🔢 Units</span><span id=\"sub_txt_levelTens\">🔟 Tens</span><span id=\"sub_txt_levelHundreds\">🏆 Hundreds</span><span id=\"sub_txt_next\">next place</span></div>",
