            {
               "text": "### The Grid\n\nBelow, we present an interactive grid that multiplies numbers using the Mesoamerican method. In the value fields, you can enter any number between 0 and 999. After entering the values, click the equal sign ( <i class=\"fa-solid fa-equals\"></i> ) to see the result.\n\nA note on the results: when the product in the grid is greater than 19, the grid does not show the number directly — it shows the operation being performed instead. To see the final result in the calculation area, click the advance (<i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrow-right\" style=\"color:#0f0; font-size: 1.2em;\"></i>) button. The steps that then appear are the simplification steps explained by Ruy D. Díaz and applied in the previous text (<htcite0>; <htcite1>):",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "38f05ff2-70fd-43da-bf0e-34a6315171c5",
                     "text": "Díaz, Ruy D.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "fa7eaa91-aafb-4974-82cb-f2a895d5c44a",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Mesoamerican sums",
                     "date_time": {
